# Golden vectors for the ustar header, written by GNU tar.
#
# Not laid out here. The archive is what this produced, GNU tar 1.35:
#
#   printf 'hello\n' > greeting.txt
#   touch -d '2026-01-01 00:00:00 UTC' greeting.txt; chmod 644 greeting.txt
#   tar --format=ustar --owner=0 --group=0 --numeric-owner \
#       -cf greeting.tar greeting.txt
#
# Three spellings of a `[padded]` number are in this one header, which is
# why it is worth having: `mode` is "0000644" and a NUL, `chksum` is
# "010342", a NUL and a space, and `devmajor` and `devminor` are eight NULs
# each -- no digits at all, which every tar reader takes as zero (26.948).
#
# `chksum` is 4322, and the 512 bytes add up to that with its own eight read as
# spaces; nothing below checks it, which the schema says.
#
# ENTRY ONE, 1024 bytes: the header, "hello\n", and 506 zero bytes to the
# end of the block. The archive's two zero blocks and GNU's padding to 10240
# bytes follow it and are not an entry.


